/-!
# Centerlessness in the original natural G₂(2) branch

The shifted involution's normal closure centralizes Z(U) and has nontrivial
hatted image. The self-centralizing simple G₂(2) derived group therefore
lies in that image. Its rank-two cubic subgroup and outer two-group absorb
every cubic of H into C_H(Z(U)): the kernel on this centralizer lies in
O₂(H), while the whole hatted kernel need not be a two-group.

The actual point residual is generated by its cubic elements, since its
quotient by O₂ is C₃. It centralizes Z(U), hence the original involution e.
The plane parabolic also centralizes e. Its conjugates of the point residual
generate L, contradicting the already proved central-seed exclusion. All
subgroups, quotient maps, and natural markings are those of the original
flag. The final theorem applies this centerlessness result to LocalStructure,
retaining only its independently produced ActionStructure premise.

The solvable Goldschmidt branch and exhaustive earlier action alternatives
remain required for full source_centerless. No result assuming centerlessness
is used in this proof. Source: Aschbacher--Smith 14.3.25,29--31, pp.1001--1003,
and the outer-two branch of A.3.18, pp.51--53. The concrete G₂ facts retain
the licensed ATLAS attribution in their Theory modules.
-/

public noncomputable section
